        "date": "2026-11-26T20:09:38Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(ui): every input on the operation pages has an accessible name\n\nA property row now opens while it draws its controls, and the seam's\nfields inside it (num and its variants, value_with_unit, combo,\ncombo_owned, tool_combo, drag_row) take the row's label as their name.\nThe operation header names its Tool, Source, Setup and Coolant combos\nby their row labels, and the Spindle speed field is named by its row.\nOn main, 1,840 of 1,861 input occurrences on the operation pages had no\nname.\n\nThe *_row field variants are now the same field as their bases, so no\nfield carries one label twice. The row-naming helpers live in the new\nlayout/row_name.rs.\n\nTests that found a row's text with get_by_label now ask for the Label\nnode, because the row's control carries the same name.\n\nStacked on the 2D slice of #1122 (#4221), which names five of the\nfields.\n\nPinned by every_operation_page_tab_names_every_input.\n\nRefs #1119\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
